{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And Esav said in his heart</b> — Rabbi Avraham [Ibn Ezra] (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 27:41) said that it is possible he revealed his secret to one of his friends. But there is no need for this, for the settling of a matter in a person's mind is called 'speaking with the heart,' even when it involves speech on the lips. Thus: 'They speak with a heart and a heart' (Psalms 12:3), for the will is called 'heart': 'And all Israel were of one heart to make David king' (1 Chronicles 12:39) — they were all of one accord and would speak of it. Likewise: 'And Yarov'am said in his heart' (1 Kings 12:26). And similarly Eliezer said (Genesis 24:45), 'I had not yet finished speaking to my heart' — yet there was a prayer on his lips: 'And he said, YHWH, Elohim of my master Avraham' (v. 12) — but 'I had not yet finished speaking to my heart' means: I had not yet completed what had arisen in my mind. So here it says that when great hatred came into the soul of Esav to hate Ya'akov over the blessing, there arose in his heart the thought that he would kill his brother, and he found comfort in this from the evil of his heart. And this is the meaning of 'And the words of Esav were told to Rivka' — therefore she said, 'He comforts himself concerning you' (v. 42). And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Genesis 27:42) that by the holy spirit it was told to her what Esav was pondering in his heart, and similarly in Bereshit Rabbah (Bereshit Rabbah 67:9). If so, 'the words of Esav' means his thoughts with the heart, as in 'I spoke, I, with my heart' (Ecclesiastes 1:16). Now, Esav was saying, 'Let the days of mourning for my father draw near,' for during his lifetime he would not distress him, or out of fear lest he curse him and his blessing turn into a curse. And Rivka feared lest the old man die suddenly and he kill him, or lest an opportunity present itself during his lifetime and he kill him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:09.834239084Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}